<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ramón Bonifaz</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">13th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ramón Bonifaz was a merchant of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burgos">Burgos</a> who commanded the fleet of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferdinand-iii-of-castile">Ferdinand III of Castile</a> at the siege of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seville">Seville</a> and is regarded as the first admiral of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile">Castile</a>. In May 1248 his ships broke the pontoon bridge linking Seville to Triana, cutting the city's supply line, and Seville surrendered later that year.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ramon-bonifaz.jpg" alt="Ramón Bonifaz" width="306" height="399" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ramon_de_Boniface_on_horse.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
